  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Virginia's 5th Congressional District will determine who represents the district covering much of rural Southside Virginia including Charlottesville, Danville, and Lynchburg. Incumbent Republican John McGuire, first elected in 2024 after defeating then-incumbent Bob Good in a competitive primary, faces a Republican primary challenge from Marine Corps veteran and real estate business owner Melanie Lucero. On the Democratic side, former U.S. Representative Tom Perriello (2009\u20132011) is seeking a comeback and faces family physician Suzanne Krzyzanowski and writer and commentator Rob Tracinski in the August 4 primary. The race takes place under Virginia's current congressional map after a state Supreme Court ruling blocked a redistricting amendment, and the district is rated as leaning Republican by nonpartisan analysts.",
